  "title": "Red Hat Security Advisory: php:8.3 security, bug fix, and enhancement update",
  "description": "A critical security update for PHP 8.3 on Red Hat Enterprise Linux 9 addresses multiple vulnerabilities including remote code execution, local privilege escalation, cross-site scripting, request smuggling, use-after-free, and denial of service issues. These flaws affect various PHP components such as PHP-CGI, PHP-FPM, PHAR, SOAP, and session handling. The update rebases PHP to version 8.3.37 and fixes these security issues to prevent potential exploitation.",
